 "result_text": "I changed the Data Format 3 check in `_get_data_format_3` (`ruuvitag_sensor/ruuvi.py`) so it no longer fails on data from RuuviFW 1.2.8. The 15 existing tests pass, but I didn't add a test for trimmed data and didn't try it against a real tag.\n\nThe old check required the raw data to be exactly 54 characters, so a payload with its trailing NULLs trimmed was rejected. It now accepts anything from 18 to 54 characters (still checking for the `03` format marker). It pads shorter input with zeros back to 54 before returning the data.\n\nI didn't touch the Data Format 2/4 parsing. I also didn't implement #29, which the issue mentions.",
